      "file_path": "app/controllers/users_controller.rb",
      "line_number": 6,
      "line_end": 6,
      "title": "SQL injection in email search",
      "description": "The index action interpolates params[:q] directly into the where SQL string. Any authenticated caller controls the query text. An authenticated user can read any column of any table, including api_token values. That user can then impersonate admins. Pass params[:q] as a bound parameter and escape LIKE wildcards with sanitize_sql_like.",
      "suggested_change": "    users = users.where(\"email LIKE ?\", \"%#{User.sanitize_sql_like(params[:q])}%\") if params[:q].present?",
      "source": "semgrep:ruby.rails.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The index action interpolates params[:q] directly into the where SQL string. Any authenticated caller controls the query text.",
      "consequence": "An authenticated user can read any column of any table, including api_token values. That user can then impersonate admins.",
      "fix": "Pass params[:q] as a bound parameter and escape LIKE wildcards with sanitize_sql_like."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
